packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:29:You can place your config in a couple of different locations and they have a
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:36:Configuration files are merged together, not replaced. Settings from the following config locations are combined. Later configs override earlier ones only for conflicting keys. Non-conflicting settings from all configs are preserved.
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:38:For example, if your global config sets `autoupdate: true` and your project config sets `model: "anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5"`, the final configuration will include both settings.
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:46:1. **Remote config** (from `.well-known/opencode`) - organizational defaults
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:47:2. **Global config** (`~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`) - user preferences
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:48:3. **Custom config** (`OPENCODE_CONFIG` env var) - custom overrides
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:49:4. **Project config** (`opencode.json` in project) - project-specific settings
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:50:5. **`.opencode` directories** - agents, commands, plugins
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:51:6. **Inline config** (`OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT` env var) - runtime overrides
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:53:This means project configs can override global defaults, and global configs can override remote organizational defaults.
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:56:The `.opencode` and `~/.config/opencode` directories use **plural names** for subdirectories: `agents/`, `commands/`, `modes/`, `plugins/`, `skills/`, `tools/`, and `themes/`. Singular names (e.g., `agent/`) are also supported for backwards compatibility.
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:63:Organizations can provide default configuration via the `.well-known/opencode` endpoint. This is fetched automatically when you authenticate with a provider that supports it.
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:65:Remote config is loaded first, serving as the base layer. All other config sources (global, project) can override these defaults.
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:69:```json title="Remote config from .well-known/opencode"
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:81:You can enable specific servers in your local config:
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:83:```json title="opencode.json"
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:99:Place your global OpenCode config in `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`. Use global config for user-wide server/runtime preferences like providers, models, and permissions.
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:101:For TUI-specific settings, use `~/.config/opencode/tui.json`.
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:103:Global config overrides remote organizational defaults.
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:109:Add `opencode.json` in your project root. Project config has the highest precedence among standard config files - it overrides both global and remote configs.
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:114:Place project specific config in the root of your project.
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:117:When OpenCode starts up, it looks for a config file in the current directory or traverse up to the nearest Git directory.
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:125:Specify a custom config file path using the `OPENCODE_CONFIG` environment variable.
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:128:export OPENCODE_CONFIG=/path/to/my/custom-config.json
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:132:Custom config is loaded between global and project configs in the precedence order.
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:138:Specify a custom config directory using the `OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR`
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:139:environment variable. This directory will be searched for agents, commands,
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:144:export OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR=/path/to/my/config-directory
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:148:The custom directory is loaded after the global config and `.opencode` directories, so it **can override** their settings.
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:154:The server/runtime config schema is defined in [**`opencode.ai/config.json`**](https://opencode.ai/config.json).
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:156:TUI config uses [**`opencode.ai/tui.json`**](https://opencode.ai/tui.json).
packages/web/src/content/docs/config.mdx:177:Use `OPENCODE_TUI_CONFIG` to point to a custom TUI config file.
