packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:2:title: Windows (WSL)
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:3:description: Run OpenCode on Windows using WSL for the best experience.
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:8:While OpenCode can run directly on Windows, we recommend using [Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/install) for the best experience. WSL provides a Linux environment that works seamlessly with OpenCode's features.
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:10::::tip[Why WSL?]
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:11:WSL offers better file system performance, full terminal support, and compatibility with development tools that OpenCode relies on.
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:20:1. **Install WSL**
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:22:   If you haven't already, [install WSL](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/install) using the official Microsoft guide.
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:24:2. **Install OpenCode in WSL**
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:26:   Once WSL is set up, open your WSL terminal and install OpenCode using one of the [installation methods](/docs/).
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:32:3. **Use OpenCode from WSL**
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:34:   Navigate to your project directory (access Windows files via `/mnt/c/`, `/mnt/d/`, etc.) and run OpenCode.
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:45:## Desktop App + WSL Server
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:47:If you prefer using the OpenCode Desktop app but want to run the server in WSL:
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:49:1. **Start the server in WSL** with `--hostname 0.0.0.0` to allow external connections:
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:58:If `localhost` does not work in your setup, connect using the WSL IP address instead (from WSL: `hostname -I`) and use `http://<wsl-ip>:4096`.
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:71:## Web Client + WSL
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:73:For the best web experience on Windows:
packages/web/src/content/docs/windows-wsl.mdx:75:1. **Run `opencode web` in the WSL terminal** rather than PowerShell:
