  1238	- `lmstudio` is the custom provider ID. This can be any string you want.
  1239	- `npm` specifies the package to use for this provider. Here, `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` is used for any OpenAI-compatible API.
  1240	- `name` is the display name for the provider in the UI.
  1241	- `options.baseURL` is the endpoint for the local server.
  1242	- `models` is a map of model IDs to their configurations. The model name will be displayed in the model selection list.
  1243	
  1244	---
  1245	
  1246	### Moonshot AI
  1247	
  1248	To use Kimi K2 from Moonshot AI:
  1249	
  1250	1. Head over to the [Moonshot AI console](https://platform.moonshot.ai/console), create an account, and click **Create API key**.
  1251	
  1252	2. Run the `/connect` command and search for **Moonshot AI**.
  1253	
  1254	   ```txt
  1255	   /connect
  1256	   ```
  1257	
  1258	3. Enter your Moonshot API key.
  1259	
  1260	   ```txt
  1261	   ┌ API key
  1262	   │
  1263	   │
  1264	   └ enter
  1265	   ```
  1266	
  1267	4. Run the `/models` command to select _Kimi K2_.
  1268	
  1269	   ```txt
  1270	   /models
  1271	   ```
  1272	
  1273	---
  1274	
  1275	### MiniMax
  1276	
  1277	1. Head over to the [MiniMax API Console](https://platform.minimax.io/login), create an account, and generate an API key.
  1278	
  1279	2. Run the `/connect` command and search for **MiniMax**.
  1280	
  1281	   ```txt
  1282	   /connect
  1283	   ```
  1284	
  1285	3. Enter your MiniMax API key.
  1286	
  1287	   ```txt
  1288	   ┌ API key
  1289	   │
  1290	   │
  1291	   └ enter
  1292	   ```
  1293	
  1294	4. Run the `/models` command to select a model like _M2.1_.
  1295	
  1296	   ```txt
  1297	   /models
  1298	   ```
  1299	
  1300	---
  1301	
  1302	### Nebius Token Factory
  1303	
  1304	1. Head over to the [Nebius Token Factory console](https://tokenfactory.nebius.com/), create an account, and click **Add Key**.
  1305	
  1306	2. Run the `/connect` command and search for **Nebius Token Factory**.
  1307	
  1308	   ```txt
  1309	   /connect
  1310	   ```
  1311	
  1312	3. Enter your Nebius Token Factory API key.
  1313	
  1314	   ```txt
  1315	   ┌ API key
  1316	   │
  1317	   │
  1318	   └ enter
  1319	   ```
  1320	
  1321	4. Run the `/models` command to select a model like _Kimi K2 Instruct_.
  1322	
  1323	   ```txt
  1324	   /models
  1325	   ```
  1326	
  1327	---
  1328	
  1329	### Ollama
  1330	
  1331	You can configure opencode to use local models through Ollama.
  1332	
  1333	:::tip
  1334	Ollama can automatically configure itself for OpenCode. See the [Ollama integration docs](https://docs.ollama.com/integrations/opencode) for details.
  1335	:::
  1336	
  1337	```json title="opencode.json" "ollama" {5, 6, 8, 10-14}
  1338	{
  1339	  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  1340	  "provider": {
  1341	    "ollama": {
  1342	      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
  1343	      "name": "Ollama (local)",
  1344	      "options": {
  1345	        "baseURL": "http://localhost:11434/v1"
  1346	      },
  1347	      "models": {
  1348	        "llama2": {
  1349	          "name": "Llama 2"
  1350	        }
  1351	      }
  1352	    }
  1353	  }
  1354	}
  1355	```
  1356	
  1357	In this example:
  1358	
  1359	- `ollama` is the custom provider ID. This can be any string you want.
  1360	- `npm` specifies the package to use for this provider. Here, `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` is used for any OpenAI-compatible API.
  1361	- `name` is the display name for the provider in the UI.
  1362	- `options.baseURL` is the endpoint for the local server.
  1363	- `models` is a map of model IDs to their configurations. The model name will be displayed in the model selection list.
  1364	
  1365	:::tip
  1366	If tool calls aren't working, try increasing `num_ctx` in Ollama. Start around 16k - 32k.
  1367	:::
  1368	
  1369	---
  1370	
  1371	### Ollama Cloud
  1372	
  1373	To use Ollama Cloud with OpenCode:
  1374	
  1375	1. Head over to [https://ollama.com/](https://ollama.com/) and sign in or create an account.
  1376	
  1377	2. Navigate to **Settings** > **Keys** and click **Add API Key** to generate a new API key.
  1378	
  1379	3. Copy the API key for use in OpenCode.
  1380	
  1381	4. Run the `/connect` command and search for **Ollama Cloud**.
  1382	
  1383	   ```txt
  1384	   /connect
  1385	   ```

