    30	---
    31	
    32	## Install
    33	
    34	The easiest way to install OpenCode is through the install script.
    35	
    36	```bash
    37	curl -fsSL https://opencode.ai/install | bash
    38	```
    39	
    40	You can also install it with the following commands:
    41	
    42	- **Using Node.js**
    43	
    44	        <Tabs>
    45	
    46	      <TabItem label="npm">
    47	      ```bash
    48	      npm install -g opencode-ai
    49	      ```
    50	
    51	          </TabItem>
    52	
    53	        <TabItem label="Bun">
    54	        ```bash
    55	        bun install -g opencode-ai
    56	        ```
    57	
    58	          </TabItem>
    59	
    60	        <TabItem label="pnpm">
    61	        ```bash
    62	        pnpm install -g opencode-ai
    63	        ```
    64	
    65	          </TabItem>
    66	
    67	        <TabItem label="Yarn">
    68	        ```bash
    69	        yarn global add opencode-ai
    70	        ```
    71	
    72	      </TabItem>
    73	
    74	  </Tabs>
    75	
    76	- **Using Homebrew on macOS and Linux**
    77	
    78	  ```bash
    79	  brew install anomalyco/tap/opencode
    80	  ```
    81	
    82	  > We recommend using the OpenCode tap for the most up to date releases. The official `brew install opencode` formula is maintained by the Homebrew team and is updated less frequently.
    83	
    84	- **Installing on Arch Linux**
    85	
    86	  ```bash
    87	  sudo pacman -S opencode           # Arch Linux (Stable)
    88	  paru -S opencode-bin              # Arch Linux (Latest from AUR)
    89	  ```
    90	
    91	#### Windows
    92	
    93	:::tip[Recommended: Use WSL]
    94	For the best experience on Windows, we recommend using [Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL)](/docs/windows-wsl). It provides better performance and full compatibility with OpenCode's features.
    95	:::
    96	
    97	- **Using Chocolatey**
    98	
    99	  ```bash
   100	  choco install opencode
   101	  ```
   102	
   103	- **Using Scoop**
   104	
   105	  ```bash
   106	  scoop install opencode
   107	  ```
   108	
   109	- **Using NPM**
   110	
   111	  ```bash
   112	  npm install -g opencode-ai
   113	  ```
   114	
   115	- **Using Mise**
   116	
   117	  ```bash
   118	  mise use -g github:anomalyco/opencode
   119	  ```
   120	
   121	- **Using Docker**
   122	
   123	  ```bash
   124	  docker run -it --rm ghcr.io/anomalyco/opencode
   125	  ```
   126	
   127	Support for installing OpenCode on Windows using Bun is currently in progress.
   128	
   129	You can also grab the binary from the [Releases](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/releases).
   130	
   131	---
   132	
   133	## Configure
   134	
   135	With OpenCode you can use any LLM provider by configuring their API keys.

